  - continual learning
  - active learning
  - metaplasticity
  - uncertainty quantification
  - edge AI
  - JAX
abstract: >-
  BiMU (Binary Metaplasticity from Uncertainty) is a Bayesian continual-learning
  rule for binary neural networks. It prevents mean-field Bernoulli posteriors from
  saturating on long non-stationary streams, which keeps epistemic uncertainty informative
  and enables fully online, buffer-free active querying via Monte Carlo disagreement.
